<title>HONG KONG: Johnson Electric year net up 58.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Johnson Electric year net up 58.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   114.6    vs  72.2</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    19.0     vs  17.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil	vs  13.94 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    437.27   vs  275.10</p>
<p>    Turnover		     2,603.32 vs  2,202.21</p>
<p>    Company name		 Johnson Electric Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  August 5-12</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   August 15</p>
<p>NOTE - Johnson Electric designs and manufactures micro-motors.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one new share for every five shares held.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 27 H.K. cents (including interim of eight cents) vs 25 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368.  http://www.hk97.com</p>
